{"key": "[\"The Pratiharas, the Palas and the Rashtrakutas fight over Kannauj, and none of them holds the north for good. In the south the Cholas take northern Sri Lanka and send a fleet against Srivijaya. Raiders come from Ghazni. After Tarain in 1192, Ghurid commanders take Delhi, and a sultanate rises there that will pass through five dynasties. It reaches further south than any northern state before it, and loses that south within a generation. Then, in 1398, Timur comes.\", \"sarvam:varun_en_suspense@en-IN\", \"+6%\", \"+0Hz\", {}, \"fx5\"]", "mp3": "/Users/saidevdhal/Desktop/Codes/indianepics/public/audio/en/medieval.mp3", "duration": 33.921958, "words": [{"t": 0.0, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "The"}, {"t": 0.42939187341772145, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "Pratiharas,"}, {"t": 0.8587837468354429, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "the"}, {"t": 1.2881756202531642, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "Palas"}, {"t": 1.7175674936708858, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "and"}, {"t": 2.1469593670886074, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "the"}, {"t": 2.5763512405063285, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "Rashtrakutas"}, {"t": 3.00574311392405, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "fight"}, {"t": 3.4351349873417716, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "over"}, {"t": 3.864526860759493, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "Kannauj,"}, {"t": 4.293918734177215, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "and"}, {"t": 4.723310607594936, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "none"}, {"t": 5.152702481012657, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "of"}, {"t": 5.582094354430379, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "them"}, {"t": 6.0114862278481, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "holds"}, {"t": 6.440878101265822, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "the"}, {"t": 6.870269974683543, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "north"}, {"t": 7.299661848101264, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "for"}, {"t": 7.729053721518986, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "good."}, {"t": 8.158445594936708, "d": 0.42939187341772145, "w": "In"}, {"t": 8.58783746835443, "d